  concept: "Authored objective: LED Resistor Voltage.\nAuthored requirement: BACKUP
    snapshot: voltage across the 330 ohm LED resistor indicates the LED branch is
    active. voltage \u2265 0.6 V. voltage \u2264 3.8 V. Connection pair R_LED_Input
    and R_LED_Output.\nGeneral teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode and
    cathode; correct polarity and suitable current control matter for normal forward
    operation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective
    is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
